From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: GPIO_FINGER off, AUD pin controller
 bus clock

GPIO_FINGER (gpd5, 0x14cb0000) belongs to the secure world: reading it
aborts, and pm_test=platform oopsed on it in samsung_pinctrl_suspend()
(the faulting page maps 0x14cb0000).  The vendor kernel skips that bank
in its save and restore when the fingerprint sensor is secure
(ENABLE_SENSORS_FPRINT_SECURE) and gives its controller no suspend hook.
Nothing in Linux uses gpd5.  This belongs in the daily device tree too.

The AUD pin controller gets its bus clock, since exynos-lpass gates the
AUD clocks in the same late phase.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts     | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
index bd77dfe07..5ca681742 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
@@ -1093,3 +1093,29 @@ gpu-abb {
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-modem.dtsi"
 /* SS333 modem node (sec_modem_v1.ko) and SPI4 boot link: same rules. */
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-modem-ss333.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * System sleep: samsung_pinctrl_suspend() reads every bank of every pin
+ * controller in the late phase.  GPIO_FINGER (gpd5, the fingerprint
+ * sensor's SPI) belongs to the secure world here: its bus clock runs, yet
+ * a read from Linux ends in a synchronous external abort (the faulting
+ * page maps 0x14cb0000; pm_test=platform, 2026-11-05).  Stock skips that
+ * bank everywhere, its sleep save and restore included, and gives
+ * controller 4 no suspend hook when the fingerprint is secure
+ * (ENABLE_SENSORS_FPRINT_SECURE, CONFIG_SENSORS_FP_SPI_GPIO="gpd5";
+ * drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-samsung.c:1450, :1496; pinctrl-exynos.c:1551).
+ * Nothing in Linux uses gpd5.
+ */
+&pinctrl_finger {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The AUD banks' own bus clock, which the driver holds around every
+ * register access: exynos-lpass gates the AUD clocks in the same late
+ * phase.
+ */
+&pinctrl_aud {
+	clocks = <&cmu_aud CLK_PCLK_GPIO_AUD>;
+	clock-names = "pclk";
+};
